&lt;div&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;div&gt;Come work alongside some of the most accomplished minds in the industry. Beyond providing competitive salaries, we’re providing a community for innovators who want to make an immediate and significant impact. If you are driven to create a better, more sustainable future, then this is the right place for you.&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p style=&quot;margin: 0in; font-family: Calibri; font-size: 11.0pt;&quot;&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The Manufacturing Technician will play a key role in supporting the manufacturing and assembly of systems across various production areas. This position requires a hands-on technician with a strong technical background, capable of executing process checks, equipment maintenance, and quality inspections while ensuring alignment with production standards.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Technicians in this role will work closely with Manufacturing Engineers and cross-functional teams to support equipment functionality, process stability, and documentation such as Work Instructions, PFMEA, and the Bill of Process (BoP). The ideal candidate is proactive, detail-oriented, and confident in troubleshooting production issues and contributing to continuous improvement initiatives.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Key Responsibilities:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Provide day-to-day support on production lines, ensuring process adherence and responding to equipment or process issues in a timely manner.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Operate and troubleshoot key production systems, including leak testers, torque tools, dispensing units, and electrical/mechanical test equipment.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Perform preventive maintenance, calibrations, and minor repairs to maintain equipment uptime and performance.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Support process development and optimization by executing tests, collecting data, and validating process parameters.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Assist with the implementation and continuous improvement of Work Instructions, PFMEA updates, and the Bill of Process.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Participate in the development and validation of new processes, tooling, and production equipment.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Monitor and analyze key production metrics such as cycle time, yield, and defect trends, escalating issues as needed.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Support product and process changes during new product introductions or line transitions.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ensure safe practices in high-voltage and high-precision assembly environments, maintaining compliance with safety and quality standards.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Maintain accurate documentation of actions performed, equipment status, and process deviations.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Key Qualifications:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Minimum 3 years of experience in an automotive or advanced manufacturing environment.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Hands-on experience with leak-testing equipment and troubleshooting methods.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Familiarity with torque and dispensing tools, test systems, and automation platforms.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Understanding of manufacturing documentation such as Work Instructions, PFMEA, and the Bill of Process.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ability to interpret technical drawings, electrical schematics, and process specifications.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong mechanical and electrical troubleshooting capabilities.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Basic experience with MES systems and data-collection tools.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Excellent communication and collaboration skills in a cross-functional team environment.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Willingness to support shift coverage, weekend work, or off-hours troubleshooting when needed.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Preferred Qualifications:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Familiarity with quality-validation methods.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Working knowledge of lean manufacturing principles, 5S, and structured problem-solving tools (e.g., 8D, DMAIC).&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Previous exposure to process audits and documentation revisions in a regulated manufacturing setting.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Physical Requirements (may include but are not limited to):&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Standing: Frequent/intermittent, up to 8 hours per day&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Walking: Frequent/intermittent, up to 8 hours per day&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Sitting: Occasional/intermittent, up to 2 hours per day&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Lifting: Up to 50 lbs occasionally/intermittently&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Carrying: Up to 50 lbs occasionally/intermittently&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Pushing/Pulling: Between 50–100 lbs occasionally/intermittently&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
