&lt;div class=&quot;content-intro&quot;&gt;&lt;div&gt;&lt;u&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Leading the future in luxury electric and mobility&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/u&gt;&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;div&gt;At Lucid, we set out to introduce the most captivating, luxury electric vehicles that elevate the human experience and transcend the perceived limitations of space, performance, and intelligence. Vehicles that are intuitive, liberating, and designed for the future of mobility.&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;div&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;div&gt;We plan to lead in this new era of luxury electric by returning to the fundamentals of great design – where every decision we make is in service of the individual and environment. Because when you are no longer bound by convention, you are free to define your own experience.&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;div&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;div&gt;Come work alongside some of the most accomplished minds in the industry. Beyond providing competitive salaries, we’re providing a community for innovators who want to make an immediate and significant impact. If you are driven to create a better, more sustainable future, then this is the right place for you.&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Lucid Motors is searching for a Plant Floor Systems (PFS) Engineer who will be based in Casa Grande, AZ location. The PFS Engineer will be responsible for monitoring, assessing the functionality, improvements, and maintaining MES in the plant.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;You Will:&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Integrating, operating, and maintaining the entire Manufacturing Execution Systems (MES) in the plant.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Work with the team on establishing MES design principles, practices, implementations, documentation, and maintenance procedures.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Assist with defining the objectives of MES improvements, including developing and reviewing proposals and presentations.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Work closely with manufacturing, line integrators, and vendors during installation/validation of MES.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ensure system uptime and backup for all MES (Hardware and Software) in the plant.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Work on establishing consistent metrics and data collection for continuous improvement.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Work closely with engineering to help report issues, lead project deliverables and provide status and progress reports.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Responsible for project management, timing and goals.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Provide direction to resources.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Report status of projects during regular team meetings.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;You Bring:&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Bachelor’s Degree in Information Technology/Computer Science or related degree with a minimum of 2-4 years of manufacturing experience with emphasis on IT Applications and Plant Floor Operations.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Proven experience in SCADA, IoT, or MES Systems.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Expert knowledge of SCADA Software: Ignition, Iconics, Cimplicity, or similar software.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Proficient knowledge of computer programming (SQL, OPC, HTML, JAVA, Python, C Sharp, Visual Basic).&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Understanding of PLC Programing: Rockwell, Siemens.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Understanding of HMI Development: Rockwell, Siemens.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Problem-solving skills specific to Information Technology, Network Management, and System Design.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experienced in designing and implementing Business Continuity Plans and Disaster Recovery Plans.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Analytical skills for interpreting business requirements and translating them into technical specifications.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Project management experience.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Manufacturing automotive experience, specific to one or more of the following areas: Powertrain, BIW, Paint, and/or GA.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ability to work any shifts - days, evenings and overnights.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
